r 2(6), which is 12.</p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":8,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959636,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"25da87f8","skill_cd":"S.C.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","createDate":1691007959636,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"09173-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"fc5135c2-0997-4826-b1f6-8c0d6f53e223","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"09173-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">A triangle with angle measures 30&deg;, 60&deg;, and 90&deg; has a perimeter of <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"18 plus 6, times, the square root of 3\"></span></span>. What is the length of the longest side of the triangle?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 12. It is given that the triangle has angle measures of 30&deg;, 60&deg;, and 90&deg;, and so the triangle is a special right triangle<!--EndFragment-->. The side measures of this type of special triangle are in the ratio <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 to 1 to the square root of 3\"></span>. If <span class=\"italic\">x</span> is the measure of the shortest leg, then the measure of the other leg is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the square root of 3 end root x\"></span> and the measure of the hypotenuse is 2<span class=\"italic\">x</span>. The perimeter of the triangle is given to be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"18, plus 6 times, the square root of 3, end root\"></span>, and so the equation for the perimeter can be written as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x, plus x, plus the square root of 3 end root x, equals 18, plus 6 times, the square root of 3\"></span>. Combining like terms and factoring out a common factor of <span class=\"italic\">x</span> on the left-hand side of the equation gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, 3 plus the square root of 3, close parenthesis, times x, equals 18, plus 6 times the square root of 3\"></span>. Rewriting the right-hand side of the equation by factoring out 6 gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, 3 plus the square root of 3, close parenthesis, times x, equals 6 times, open parenthesis, 3 plus the square root of 3, close parenthesis\"></span>. Dividing both sides of the equation by the common factor <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, 3 plus the square root of 3, close parenthesis\"></span> gives <span class=\"italic\">x</span> = 6. The longest side of the right triangle, the hypotenuse, has a length of 2<span class=\"italic\">x</span>, or 2(6), which is 12.</p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959636,"updateDate":1691007959636,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959636, 1691007959636),
    ($SATQ$2855cb58$SATQ$, $SATQ$93083ace-02bf-4d1e-9794-d51ec7697e04$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Circles$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane has its center at <math alttext="left parenthesis 16 comma 17 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and has a radius of <math alttext="7 k"><mrow>
	<mn>7</mn>
	<mi>k</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Which equation represents this circle?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"5091364b-164f-4662-b395-685c5910a6ab","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 16 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 17 right parenthesis squared equals 49 k\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>49</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"9ac621bd-3412-44bf-96db-4a2f3ace4379","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 16 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 17 right parenthesis squared equals 49 k squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>49</mn></mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"a38d25b0-4635-4577-b4b3-30ab1f2f4565","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 16 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 17 right parenthesis squared equals 7 k\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"2b680af7-7dad-4942-9d97-675678fecc48","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 16 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 17 right parenthesis squared equals 7 k squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9ac621bd-3412-44bf-96db-4a2f3ace4379"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The equation of a circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be written as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where the center of the circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and the radius of the circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s given that this circle has a center at <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 16 comma 17 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and a radius of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 k"><mn>7</mn><mi>k</mi></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="16"><mn>16</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h"><mi>h</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="17"><mn>17</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 k"><mn>7</mn><mi>k</mi></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> in&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 16 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 17 right parenthesis squared equals left parenthesis 7 k right parenthesis squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 16 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 17 right parenthesis squared equals 49 k squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>49</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Therefore, the equation that represents this circle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis x minus 16 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 17 right parenthesis squared equals 49 k squared"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>49</mn><msup><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This equation represents a circle with radius&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 StartRoot k EndRoot"><mn>7</mn><msqrt><mi>k</mi></msqrt></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 k"><mn>7</mn><mi>k</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This equation represents a circle with radius&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartRoot 7 k EndRoot"><msqrt><mn>7</mn><mi>k</mi></msqrt></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 k"><mn>7</mn><mi>k</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This equation represents a circle with radius&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartRoot 7 EndRoot k"><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mi>k</mi></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 k"><mn>7</mn><mi>k</mi></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"2855cb58","external_id":"93083ace-02bf-4d1e-9794-d51ec7697e04","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"84d789b1-bb6c-4cbe-9d1d-485ceef845c3","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.D.","skill_desc":"Circles","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane has its center at <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 16 comma 17 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>)</mo></math> and has a radius of <math alttext=\"7 k\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t<mi>k</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Which equation represents this circle?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"5091364b-164f-4662-b395-685c5910a6ab","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 16 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 17 right parenthesis squared equals 49 k\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>17</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>49</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></math></p>"},{"id":"9ac621bd-3412-44bf-96db-4a2f3ace4379","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 16 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 17 right parenthesis squared equals 49 k squared\"><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>y<