: center;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the figure, <math alttext=\"upper R upper T equals upper T upper U\"><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi></math>, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper V upper S upper T\"><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"29 degree\"><mn>29</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, and the measure of angle&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper R upper V upper S\"><mi>R</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"41 degree\"><mn>41</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["156"],"correct_answer":["156"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is <math alttext=\"156\"><mn>156</mn>\n</math>. In the figure shown, the sum of the measures of angle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper S\"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> and angle <math alttext=\"upper R upper V upper S\"><mi>R</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"180 degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper R upper V upper S\"><mi>R</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"41 degree\"><mn>41</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Therefore, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper S\"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 180 minus 41 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or <math alttext=\"139 degree\"><mn>139</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is <math alttext=\"180 degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. In triangle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper S\"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math>, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper S\"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"139 degree\"><mn>139</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and it's given that the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper V upper S upper T\"><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"29 degree\"><mn>29</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Thus, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper V upper U upper S\"><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 180 minus 139 minus 29 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>139</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or <math alttext=\"12 degree\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"upper R upper T equals upper T upper U\"><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi></math>. Therefore, triangle <math alttext=\"upper T upper U upper R\"><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is an isosceles triangle and the measure of <math alttext=\"upper V upper U upper S\"><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper T upper R upper U\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>U</mi></math>. In triangle <math alttext=\"upper T upper U upper R\"><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></math>, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper V upper U upper S\"><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"12 degree\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper T upper R upper U\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>U</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"12 degree\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Thus, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper U upper T upper R\"><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 180 minus 12 minus 12 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or <math alttext=\"156 degree\"><mn>156</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The figure shows that the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper U upper T upper R\"><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"x degree\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, so the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"156\"><mn>156</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357407,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"2d2cb85e","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1730147357407,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"","external_id":"8cc3132c-df20-42a0-a034-412f01a73b1e","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"28a89d12-6cf6-4223-aca8-9a9e247b3e75","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[],"externalid":"8cc3132c-df20-42a0-a034-412f01a73b1e","keys":["156"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is <math alttext=\"156\"><mn>156</mn>\n</math>. In the figure shown, the sum of the measures of angle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper S\"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> and angle <math alttext=\"upper R upper V upper S\"><mi>R</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"180 degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper R upper V upper S\"><mi>R</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"41 degree\"><mn>41</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Therefore, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper S\"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 180 minus 41 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>41</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or <math alttext=\"139 degree\"><mn>139</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The sum of the measures of the interior angles of a triangle is <math alttext=\"180 degree\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. In triangle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper S\"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math>, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper U upper V upper S\"><mi>U</mi><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"139 degree\"><mn>139</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and it's given that the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper V upper S upper T\"><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>T</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"29 degree\"><mn>29</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Thus, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper V upper U upper S\"><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 180 minus 139 minus 29 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>139</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>29</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or <math alttext=\"12 degree\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"upper R upper T equals upper T upper U\"><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi></math>. Therefore, triangle <math alttext=\"upper T upper U upper R\"><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is an isosceles triangle and the measure of <math alttext=\"upper V upper U upper S\"><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is equal to the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper T upper R upper U\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>U</mi></math>. In triangle <math alttext=\"upper T upper U upper R\"><mi>T</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>R</mi></math>, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper V upper U upper S\"><mi>V</mi><mi>U</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"12 degree\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> and the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper T upper R upper U\"><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>U</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"12 degree\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. Thus, the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper U upper T upper R\"><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 180 minus 12 minus 12 right parenthesis degree\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>180</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, or <math alttext=\"156 degree\"><mn>156</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. The figure shows that the measure of angle <math alttext=\"upper U upper T upper R\"><mi>U</mi><mi>T</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"x degree\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, so the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"156\"><mn>156</mn>\n</math>.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"323.608\" height=\"267.862\" viewBox=\"0 0 323.608 267.862\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Triangle upper R upper T upper U and triangle upper S upper V upper U. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"a2c377a2-a0c7-41f8-95e5-4674b772fcf5\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><polygon points=\"161.413 108.188 310.623 203.119 12.203 203.119 161.413 108.188\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon><polyline points=\"161.413 108.128 310.623 13.197 220.384 202.871\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polyline><path d=\"M12.2,203.691\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></path><path d=\"M318.162,210.739a5.041,5.041,0,0,1,1.1.126,4.759,4.759,0,0,1,1.114.406,2.285,2.285,0,0,1,1.25,2.1,2.863,2.863,0,0,1-.261,1.182,3.742,3.742,0,0,1-.62.978,6.007,6.007,0,0,1-.833.756,7.331,7.331,0,0,1-.805.542c-.22.124-.42.23-.6.32a.149.149,0,0,0-.1.233,22.241,22.241,0,0,0,.949,2.635,13.694,13.694,0,0,0,1.027,2.036c.065.1.129.2.193.28a1.236,1.236,0,0,0,.2.214c.07.058.135.11.193.155a.669.669,0,0,0,.2.106,1.556,1.556,0,0,1,.174.068.519.519,0,0,0,.184.039c.084.007.139.01.165.01h.349a.612.612,0,0,1,.019.542,5.753,5.753,0,0,1-1.124.1,2.469,2.469,0,0,1-2.113-1.259,20.681,20.681,0,0,1-1.9-4.574q-.1-.272-.853-.272a3.894,3.894,0,0,0-.794.049.309.309,0,0,0-.213.281l-.562,3a9.2,9.2,0,0,0-.213,1.744c0,.1.087.2.261.281a1.838,1.838,0,0,0,.514.165l.271.038c.026,0,.039.027.039.078a1,1,0,0,1-.116.446q-1.8-.1-2.016-.1-.058,0-2.132.1a.225.225,0,0,1-.039-.155c0-.246.045-.369.136-.369a2.906,2.906,0,0,0,.7-.126c.31-.083.491-.184.542-.3a12.683,12.683,0,0,0,.5-1.86l1.59-8.024a5.082,5.