    ($SATQ$3453aafc$SATQ$, $SATQ$f5e0aefd-1908-42ec-9072-52390bef3063$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$06042b73-3533-41fa-a09e-6ebf5afe22cc$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Area and volume$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">What is the area, in square centimeters, of a rectangle with a length of <math alttext="36"><mn>36</mn>
</math> centimeters and a width of <math alttext="34"><mn>34</mn>
</math> centimeters?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"752c57a8-cadc-4f75-9cd8-f19697779ceb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5ba5ae56-f7d8-46b7-b06f-350382826c64","content":"<p><math alttext=\"140\"><mn>140</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"35682da6-a92d-444e-9bd2-4fa94b3b9cef","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,156\"><mn>1,156</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"51a15440-d255-495b-b45a-a3471859a267","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,224\"><mn>1,224</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["51a15440-d255-495b-b45a-a3471859a267"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. The area <math alttext="upper A"><mi>A</mi>
</math>, in square centimeters, of a rectangle can be found using the formula <math alttext="upper A equals script l w"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> is the length, in centimeters, of the rectangle and <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> is its width, in centimeters. It's given that the rectangle has a length of <math alttext="36"><mn>36</mn>
</math> centimeters and a width of <math alttext="34"><mn>34</mn>
</math> centimeters. Substituting <math alttext="36"><mn>36</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="script l"><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi></math> and <math alttext="34"><mn>34</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="w"><mi>w</mi>
</math> in the formula <math alttext="upper A equals script l w"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="script">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math> yields <math alttext="upper A equals 36 left parenthesis 34 right parenthesis"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mfenced><mn>34</mn></mfenced></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="upper A equals 1,224"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,224</mn></math>. Therefore, the area, in square centimeters, of this rectangle is <math alttext="1,224"><mn>1,224</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the perimeter, in centimeters, not the area, in square centimeters, of the rectangle.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"3453aafc","external_id":"f5e0aefd-1908-42ec-9072-52390bef3063","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"06042b73-3533-41fa-a09e-6ebf5afe22cc","uId":"a957899c-b352-4a94-91c8-7fcade652f9d","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What is the area, in square centimeters, of a rectangle with a length of <math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>\n</math> centimeters and a width of <math alttext=\"34\"><mn>34</mn>\n</math> centimeters?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"752c57a8-cadc-4f75-9cd8-f19697779ceb","content":"<p><math alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5ba5ae56-f7d8-46b7-b06f-350382826c64","content":"<p><math alttext=\"140\"><mn>140</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"35682da6-a92d-444e-9bd2-4fa94b3b9cef","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,156\"><mn>1,156</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"51a15440-d255-495b-b45a-a3471859a267","content":"<p><math alttext=\"1,224\"><mn>1,224</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["51a15440-d255-495b-b45a-a3471859a267"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. The area <math alttext=\"upper A\"><mi>A</mi>\n</math>, in square centimeters, of a rectangle can be found using the formula <math alttext=\"upper A equals script l w\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mi>w</mi></math>, where&nbsp;<math alttext=\"script l\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></math> is the length, in centimeters, of the rectangle and <math alttext=\"w\"><mi>w</mi>\n</math> is its width, in centimeters. It's given that the rectangle has a length of <math alttext=\"36\"><mn>36</mn>