<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for right triangle" class="sr-only"><ul><li>One angle is a right angle.</li>
<li>The length of the side opposite the right angle is c.</li>
<li>The lengths of the other 2 sides are as follows:<br>
<ul>
<li>9</li>
<li>6</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In the right triangle shown, which of the following is closest to the value of <math alttext="c"><mi>c</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"71b0e81e-ca7a-4d9f-88c3-ef92e735d607","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7.5\"><mn>7.5</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f955cd93-0b31-4ce7-a433-eb552be7a884","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10.8\"><mn>10.8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"12dc5000-b0f4-4742-bd08-9b3605ad259a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e22d52f1-7c12-48bc-bd54-d9cf31697bfe","content":"<p><math alttext=\"58.5\"><mn>58.5</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["f955cd93-0b31-4ce7-a433-eb552be7a884"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. By the Pythagorean theorem, if a right triangle has a hypotenuse with length <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math> and legs with lengths <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s"><mi>s</mi></math>, then <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r squared plus s squared equals t squared"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It's given in the right triangle shown that the legs have lengths of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9"><mn>9</mn></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="6"><mn>6</mn></math> and the hypotenuse has a length of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9"><mn>9</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="6"><mn>6</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="s"><mi>s</mi></math>, and&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="t"><mi>t</mi></math> in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r squared plus s squared equals t squared"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9 squared plus 6 squared equals c squared"><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="117 equals c squared"><mn>117</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="plus or minus StartRoot 117 EndRoot equals c"><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>117</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math>. Since the length of a side of a triangle must be positive, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartRoot 117 EndRoot"><msqrt><mn>117</mn></msqrt></math>, which is approximately equal to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10.8167"><mn>10.8167</mn></math>. Of the choices,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="10.8"><mn>10.8</mn></math> is the closest to the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"36661021","external_id":"21685f5b-1a79-4984-81ee-932431a02a7a","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"b6b9e17c-6b8a-484e-96ad-2cf53c32380c","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.C.","skill_desc":"Right triangles and trigonometry","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"250.0pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 250.0 210.0\" height=\"210.0pt\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A right triangle. Refer to long description.\">\n  <g>\n    <g><defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 197.568  L 244.8 197.568  L 244.8 0  L 0 0  z \" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 190.368  L 237.6 190.368  L 237.6 7.2  L 7.2 7.2  z \" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n   <g id=\"text_1\">\n    <!-- $9$ -->\n    <defs>\n     <path d=\"M 5.90625 -2.203125  L 5.59375 -0.203125  Q 17.09375 1.796875 25.046875 9.5  Q 33 17.203125 36 29.40625  Q 30.203125 23.703125 21 23.703125  Q 12.90625 23.703125 7.953125 29.296875  Q 3 34.90625 3 44  Q 3 54.09375 8.953125 60.84375  Q 14.90625 67.59375 23.796875 67.59375  Q 33.296875 67.59375 39.5 60  Q 45.90625 52 45.90625 39.40625  Q 45.90625 30.59375 42.84375 22.84375  Q 39.796875 15.09375 33.90625 9.703125  Q 27.703125 4.09375 21.796875 1.640625  Q 15.90625 -0.796875 5.90625 -2.203125  z M 36.203125 35.5  L 