\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-32\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1049.316406\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-115\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1084.375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-99\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1123.925781\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-97\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1165.234375\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-108\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1189.746094\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-101\"></use>\n     <use x=\"1231.738281\" xlink:href=\"#CrimsonText-Regular-46\"></use>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n</g>\n    <g transform=\"translate(21, 20) scale(1 1) \"><g id=\"a0038aa6-86e3-41c5-acba-bc4617837f30\" data-name=\"Layer 1\">\n        <rect x=\"19.067\" y=\"125.685\" width=\"11.34\" height=\"11.34\" stroke-width=\"0.945\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"></rect>\n        <polygon points=\"19.067 0.945 19.067 137.025 200.507 137.025 19.067 0.945\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></polygon>\n        <text x=\"15\" y=\"165\" class=\"small\">\n            <!-- Note: Figure not drawn to scale. -->\n        </text>\n        <style>\n            .small { font: italic 13px Crimson; }\n            .heavy { font: bold 30px sans-serif; }\n\n            /* Note that the color of the text is set with the    *\n            * fill property, the color property is for HTML only */\n            .Rrrrr { font: italic 40px serif; fill: red; }\n        </style>\n    </g>\n</g>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for right triangle\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>One angle is a right angle.</li>\n<li>The length of the side opposite the right angle is c.</li>\n<li>The lengths of the other 2 sides are as follows:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>9</li>\n<li>6</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In the right triangle shown, which of the following is closest to the value of <math alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"71b0e81e-ca7a-4d9f-88c3-ef92e735d607","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7.5\"><mn>7.5</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f955cd93-0b31-4ce7-a433-eb552be7a884","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10.8\"><mn>10.8</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"12dc5000-b0f4-4742-bd08-9b3605ad259a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"15\"><mn>15</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e22d52f1-7c12-48bc-bd54-d9cf31697bfe","content":"<p><math alttext=\"58.5\"><mn>58.5</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["f955cd93-0b31-4ce7-a433-eb552be7a884"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. By the Pythagorean theorem, if a right triangle has a hypotenuse with length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> and legs with lengths <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r squared plus s squared equals t squared\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It's given in the right triangle shown that the legs have lengths of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn></math> and the hypotenuse has a length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"s\"><mi>s</mi></math>, and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r squared plus s squared equals t squared\"><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9 squared plus 6 squared equals c squared\"><msup><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mn>6</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"117 equals c squared\"><mn>117</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Taking the square root of both sides of this equation yields&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"plus or minus StartRoot 117 EndRoot equals c\"><mo>&#177;</mo><msqrt><mn>117</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math>. Since the length of a side of a triangle must be positive, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartRoot 117 EndRoot\"><msqrt><mn>117</mn></msqrt></math>, which is approximately equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10.8167\"><mn>10.8167</mn></math>. Of the choices,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"10.8\"><mn>10.8</mn></math> is the closest to the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parentt