</math>, respectively. Since corresponding angles of similar triangles are congruent, it follows that the measure of&nbsp;<math alttext="angle upper Z"><mo>∠</mo><mi>Z</mi></math> is congruent to the measure of <math alttext="angle upper T"><mo>∠</mo><mi>T</mi></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the measure of <math alttext="angle upper Z"><mo>∠</mo><mi>Z</mi></math> is <math alttext="20 degree"><mn>20</mn><mo>°</mo></math>. Therefore, the measure of <math alttext="angle upper T"><mo>∠</mo><mi>T</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext="20 degree"><mn>20</mn><mo>°</mo></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from a conceptual error.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is half the measure of <math alttext="angle upper Z"><mo>∠</mo><mi>Z</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is twice the measure of <math alttext="angle upper Z"><mo>∠</mo><mi>Z</mi></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"3b225698","external_id":"4e338dff-7649-48c0-89f7-665b5a7d5776","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"41cd3e24-859e-4498-ad48-4bf3083c8aba","uId":"52b4079a-9403-4b02-8918-d369a825a666","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>Triangle <math alttext=\"upper X upper Y upper Z\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>X</mi>\n\t<mi>Y</mi>\n\t<mi>Z</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> is similar to triangle <math alttext=\"upper R upper S upper T\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t<mi>T</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> such that <math alttext=\"upper X\"><mi>X</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper Y\"><mi>Y</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper Z\"><mi>Z</mi>\n</math> correspond to <math alttext=\"upper R\"><mi>R</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper S\"><mi>S</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"upper T\"><mi>T</mi>\n</math>, respectively. The measure of <math alttext=\"angle upper Z\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>Z</mi></math> is <math alttext=\"20 degree\"><mn>20</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math> and <math alttext=\"2 upper X upper Y equals upper R upper S\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t<mi>X</mi>\n\t\t<mi>Y</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>R</mi>\n\t\t<mi>S</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. What is the measure of <math alttext=\"angle upper T\"><mo>&#8736;</mo><mi>T</mi></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"24b9a077-30fc-454b-9146-6eb3e2701273","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2 degree\"><mn>2</mn>\n<mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"86423e87-dfa2-41c2-a865-a2c1b93f5dcd","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10 degree\"><mn>10</mn>\n<mo>&#176